# The Brain — box environment (copy to `deploy/.env`).
#
#   cp deploy/.env.example deploy/.env   # then fill in real values
#
# `.env` is gitignored. On a production box install.sh generates real values
# once into /opt/brain/deploy/.env (600 root:root) and preserves them across
# re-runs. This file is the local/dev shape + documentation of every knob.

# ------------------------------------------------------------------ public identity
# The box's canonical hostname (the DNS name you point at the box). caddy
# provisions the TLS cert for exactly this name.
BRAIN_DOMAIN=brain.example.com
# ACME account contact for cert issuance/expiry notices.
ACME_EMAIL=ops@example.com

# ------------------------------------------------------------------ postgres
# Superuser is used only by initdb, the local executor bootstrap, and pgBackRest
# on the box; it is never distributed. `brain` is the single database.
POSTGRES_SUPERUSER=postgres
POSTGRES_SUPERUSER_PASSWORD=change_me_generated_secret
BRAIN_DB=brain

# ------------------------------------------------------------------ box DB connections
# Two roles, two URLs:
#   brain_app   — DML pool for the read/write path (least-privilege).
#   brain_owner — DDL-only executor connection over the private network; NEVER
#                 handed out. Both point at the `postgres` service by name.
# host = the compose service name `postgres`; port 5432 on the private network.
BRAIN_APP_DATABASE_URL=postgres://brain_app:change_me_app_pw@postgres:5432/brain
BRAIN_OWNER_DATABASE_URL=postgres://brain_owner:change_me_owner_pw@postgres:5432/brain

# ------------------------------------------------------------------ migrations (one-off `migrate` service)
# `docker compose --profile tools run --rm migrate` needs the superuser URL (to
# create roles) + the role passwords it assigns. Same generated-once secrets as
# above; the passwords here MUST match the ones embedded in the URLs.
BRAIN_SUPERUSER_DATABASE_URL=postgres://postgres:change_me_generated_secret@postgres:5432/brain
BRAIN_OWNER_PASSWORD=change_me_owner_pw
BRAIN_APP_PASSWORD=change_me_app_pw
BRAIN_EXTERNAL_PASSWORD=change_me_external_pw

# ------------------------------------------------------------------ fleet control plane (optional)
# If you run a fleet control plane ("booth"), the box phones it for
# validate/heartbeat and the updater reads its release channel. Leave unset to
# run standalone: the box serves ungated and the updater follows GitHub
# Releases instead.
# BRAIN_BOOTH_URL=

# ------------------------------------------------------------------ oauth (claude.ai connect)
# The box's public origin. When set, the box runs its OWN OAuth authorization
# server (MCP auth spec) so a member adds https://<host>/mcp in claude.ai /
# Claude Desktop and signs in with a pasted member token — no config file.
# Absent it, only static-bearer (.mcp.json) / pre-issued JWTs work.
BRAIN_PUBLIC_URL=https://brain.example.com

# ------------------------------------------------------------------ image pinning (prod)
# In prod the updater sets these to the signed, digest-pinned release —
# every component, not just the app. Locally, leave them
# unset: BRAIN_IMAGE builds from source, postgres builds from deploy/postgres,
# caddy falls back to the in-repo digest pin in docker-compose.yml.
# BRAIN_IMAGE=ghcr.io/maslow-tech/maslow/box@sha256:<digest>
# BRAIN_UPDATER_IMAGE=ghcr.io/maslow-tech/maslow/updater@sha256:<digest>
# BRAIN_POSTGRES_IMAGE=ghcr.io/maslow-tech/maslow/postgres@sha256:<digest>
# BRAIN_CADDY_IMAGE=docker.io/library/caddy@sha256:<digest>

# base64 PEM of an EC P-256 private key that signs OAuth access tokens. Set in
# prod so tokens survive box restarts (and validate across replicas). Absent it,
# the box generates an ephemeral per-process key and logs a warning (dev only).
# BRAIN_OAUTH_SIGNING_KEY_B64=<base64 of an ES256 private-key PEM>

# ------------------------------------------------------------------ updater
# The box's fleet token (only meaningful with BRAIN_BOOTH_URL set). Used by
# the box for validate/heartbeat and by the updater for heartbeat + releases.
# BRAIN_TOKEN=change_me_fleet_token
# First-boot baseline for the updater's state (what release this box was
# installed with). install.sh writes it; ignored once the updater has state.
# BRAIN_CURRENT_VERSION=v0.1.0
# Where the fleet pulls box images from (the updater appends @sha256:<digest>).
# BRAIN_IMAGE_REPO=ghcr.io/maslow-tech/maslow/box
# Standalone release feed: the GitHub repo whose Releases the updater follows
# when no booth is configured. install.sh writes the default.
# BRAIN_RELEASES_REPO=maslow-tech/maslow
# BRAIN_RELEASE_CHANNEL=stable
# Poll interval override in ms (defaults: 3 min booth mode, 15 min GitHub feed).
# BRAIN_UPDATER_POLL_MS=
# The HOST path of this deploy directory. The updater mounts it at the SAME
# path inside its container so compose-resolved bind mounts stay host-valid.
# BRAIN_HOST_DEPLOY_DIR=/opt/brain/deploy

# ------------------------------------------------------------------ backups
# The `backup` compose sidecar takes pgBackRest full backups on a schedule and
# expires old ones. Every value below has a working default — set them only to
# trade PITR window against disk. See docs/runbooks/pitr.md.
#
# Cadence + retention: 12h x 4 fulls => a ~48h PITR window. Fulls are cheap (the
# database is tens of MB); RETAINED WAL is the entire cost, so a SHORT full
# cadence is what keeps the repo small.
# BRAIN_BACKUP_INTERVAL_HOURS=12
# BRAIN_BACKUP_RETENTION_FULL=4
# Repo budget as a percent of the volume, computed at runtime — 20% is ~10 GiB
# on a 50 G box, ~16 GiB on an 80 G one. Crossing it expires harder (4->3->2->1)
# and then refuses the backup rather than filling the disk.
# BRAIN_BACKUP_REPO_BUDGET_PCT=20
# Absolute free-space floor before a backup may start.
# BRAIN_BACKUP_MIN_FREE_MB=2048
# How often the scheduler wakes up to check the schedule / run expire.
# BRAIN_BACKUP_POLL_SECONDS=300

# The read-only write-shed threshold. SHARED, deliberately: the box app refuses
# content writes past it AND the backup scheduler refuses to add backups past
# it. One number, one meaning.
# BRAIN_WRITE_SHED_PCT=90
